<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:layout_width="match_parent" android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="#000" android:keepScreenOn="true">
    <com.google.vr.sdk.base.GvrView
        android:id="@+id/glView"
        android:layout_width="match_parent" android:layout_height="match_parent" />
    <!-- Web mode: the page lives here and is copied into a GL texture
         (PixelCopy) for the flat screen. It stays visible on the phone
         screen as a mirror; inside the headset you never see it.

         1600x900 (16:9), deliberately. 1440x900 (16:10) was tried because it
         is less letterboxy and cheaper to read back, but it narrows the CSS
         viewport from 609 to 548 px, and sites have real breakpoints in that
         range. Measured on one consent-walled site:

             1600x900 -> viewport 609x343 -> document 1012/343  (scrolls)
             1440x900 -> viewport 548x343 -> document  343/343  (no scroller)

         At 548px the same page collapses to a document that exactly fits,
         with its content in a wrapper that has overflow-y:visible and so no
         scroll mechanism whatsoever. PgDn and the scrollbar were not broken -
         there was nothing left to scroll, and the "I agree" button below the
         fold became unreachable. 61px of width is not worth that.

         The viewport HEIGHT is 343 CSS px at any aspect, because it is
         900 raster px over the 2.625 display density, and 900 is the window's
         content area (the display cutout and nav bar take the rest). So
         aspect only ever moves width, never height - a taller aspect
         narrows the screen rather than making it taller. -->
    <FrameLayout
        android:id="@+id/webHost"
        android:layout_width="1600px" android:layout_height="900px"
        android:layout_gravity="center" />
    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/btnClose"
        android:layout_width="30dp" android:layout_height="30dp"
        android:layout_gravity="top|start"
        android:layout_margin="8dp"
        android:background="@drawable/close_button_bg"
        android:gravity="center"
        android:text="✕" android:textSize="16sp"
        android:textColor="#fff" />
    <TextView android:id="@+id/txtStatus"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:visibility="gone" />
</FrameLayout>
